{% render 'section-style', section: section %}
{%- comment -%}
  "How it's made" and "Pour it with", rebuilt against the design.

  The design runs the numbered steps down the left in a 44px/1fr grid with the
  ingredient list ruled off beneath them, and a full-bleed process photograph
  filling the right half. The port had the steps but neither the number column
  nor the image.

  Steps come from custom.process_steps (JSON) if present, otherwise from
  custom.process, which the live store holds as prose in "HEADING - body"
  blocks separated by blank lines.

  The process image falls back through: custom.process_image, then the
  product's second media item, then its featured image — so the panel is never
  empty on a product with photography.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The bottle's code — NON1, NON3 — resolved the same way every other surface
  resolves it, so the Somm opened from a pairing tile here is told about the
  same bottle the buy box is selling. A render tag cannot live inside a liquid
  block, so this capture sits outside it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture code %}{% render 'non-code', product: product %}{% endcapture -%}
{%- assign code = code | strip -%}

{%- liquid
  assign steps = product.metafields.custom.process_steps.value
  assign prose = product.metafields.custom.process | metafield_text | strip
  assign pairings = product.metafields.custom.pairings.value
  assign ingredients = product.metafields.custom.ingredients | metafield_text

  # The section setting wins, so this panel's image can be changed in the
  # editor per template without touching product data. Below it the original
  # chain still applies, which is what keeps all 27 products populated without
  # anyone opening the editor.
  #
  # These are hash comments. A comment TAG here is a syntax error: inside a
  # liquid block the enclosing tag ends at the first closing delimiter it meets,
  # so a nested tag cuts the block short and everything after becomes stray
  # markup. Shopify then rejects the file and silently keeps serving the
  # previous version — which is exactly what happened. This section sat frozen
  # on the staging theme from 31 July through two later commits that both
  # pushed cleanly. check.py rule 1b now catches it.
  #
  # Note there are deliberately no brace-percent sequences in this comment:
  # a closing delimiter inside the prose would end the block just as surely.
  assign process_image = section.settings.image
  if process_image == blank
    assign process_image = product.metafields.custom.process_image.value
  endif
  if process_image == blank
    assign process_image = product.media[1]
  endif
  if process_image == blank
    assign process_image = product.featured_media
  endif

  assign media_ratio = section.settings.media_ratio | default: 'portrait'

  # Video, on the same ladder as the image and taking priority over it.
  #
  # These are per-bottle films, so the PRODUCT metafield is the real path --
  # product.json is one template shared by every product, so a section setting
  # would put one video on all of them, which is the same mistake the eyebrow
  # suffix made when it printed an ABV on a metal stopper.
  #
  # Two shapes arrive depending on where the file was uploaded, and both are
  # handled at the markup below rather than normalised here:
  #   Shopify FILES  -- a generic file, addressed by .url
  #   product MEDIA  -- a video object carrying .sources
  # The image is still resolved above and becomes the poster frame, so the
  # panel is never empty while a video buffers and never breaks if one is
  # missing.
  assign process_video = section.settings.video
  if process_video == blank
    assign process_video = product.metafields.custom.process_video.value
  endif
  if process_video == blank
    for item in product.media
      if item.media_type == 'video'
        assign process_video = item
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign process_video_url = section.settings.video_url
  if process_video_url == blank
    assign process_video_url = product.metafields.custom.process_video_url | metafield_text
  endif

  # YouTube is a different animal to a file: it is an iframe, not a video
  # element, so object-fit cannot crop it and the player draws its own chrome.
  # Pull the id out of whichever of the three URL shapes was pasted.
  assign yt_id = ''
  if process_video_url contains 'youtube.com/watch'
    assign yt_id = process_video_url | split: 'v=' | last | split: '&' | first
  elsif process_video_url contains 'youtu.be/'
    assign yt_id = process_video_url | split: 'youtu.be/' | last | split: '?' | first
  elsif process_video_url contains '/embed/'
    assign yt_id = process_video_url | split: '/embed/' | last | split: '?' | first
  endif
  assign yt_id = yt_id | strip
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  INGREDIENTS, on a phone, with the method rather than with the photographs.

  The list sits under the gallery on a desktop, where the buy column is taller
  than the pictures and it fills space that would be empty. On a phone the two
  columns become one, so "under the gallery" put an ingredient list between the
  photographs and the product's own name.

  It reads here instead — the brief groups it with how the bottle is made — and
  the gallery copy is hidden at this width. Two elements, exactly one of them
  in the document at a time: display:none takes the other out of the
  accessibility tree as well as off the screen.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if ingredients != blank -%}
  <div class="non-ingr non-ingr--mobile">
    <div class="non-spec__k">{{ section.settings.ingredients_label }}</div>
    <p class="non-ingr__list">{{ ingredients }}</p>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if steps != blank or prose != blank -%}
  <div class="non-process">
    <div class="non-process__copy">
      <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.steps_heading }}</div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Three sources, in priority order: Step blocks, then the process_steps
        JSON metafield, then the prose metafield split on blank lines.

        Blocks come first so the section is editable at all — it had no block
        types, so the theme editor offered two headings and nothing else while
        the five visible steps came from per-product data with no way to touch
        them from here.

        Blocks are an OVERRIDE, not a replacement. Step copy is genuinely
        per-product — NON1's raspberries are not NON5's hibiscus — so the
        metafield stays the default and blocks win only where someone has
        deliberately added them. Adding a Step block to the default product
        template would otherwise give all nine bottles the same process.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign step_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'step' -%}

      <div class="non-steps">
        {%- if step_blocks.size > 0 -%}
          {%- for block in step_blocks -%}
            <div class="non-step" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <div class="non-step__n">
                {{- block.settings.number | default: forloop.index | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 -}}
              </div>
              <div>
                <div class="non-step__t">{{ block.settings.title }}</div>
                <p class="non-step__b">{{ block.settings.body }}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}

        {%- elsif steps != blank -%}
          {%- for step in steps -%}
            <div class="non-step">
              <div class="non-step__n">{{ step.n }}</div>
              <div>
                <div class="non-step__t">{{ step.title }}</div>
                <p class="non-step__b">{{ step.body }}</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}

        {%- else -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Split on the SECTION KEYWORDS, not on blank lines.

            Checked every bottle against the live store: NON1 is the only one
            whose custom.process separates sections with a blank line. NON2,
            NON3, NON5 and NON7 use a single newline. Splitting on a blank line
            therefore gave NON1 five steps and every other bottle exactly one —
            the whole process crushed into step 01 "Fruit" with "TANNIN -",
            "SALINITY -" and the rest buried mid-paragraph. That is what made
            the other PDPs look nothing like NON1: the theme was correct only
            for the one product whose data happened to match the parser.

            Keying on the keywords makes the parse independent of how the prose
            is typed, so a merchandiser reformatting a metafield cannot silently
            collapse a product's process again. A product using none of the
            keywords falls back to the old blank-line split.

            &nbsp; is stripped because NON3 and NON5 hold it literally — it was
            rendering as the visible characters "&nbsp;" mid-sentence.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign norm = prose | replace: '&nbsp;', ' '
            assign norm = norm | replace: '&amp;nbsp;', ' '
            assign norm = norm | replace: 'FRUIT - ', '~~FRUIT - '
            assign norm = norm | replace: 'TANNIN - ', '~~TANNIN - '
            assign norm = norm | replace: 'SALINITY - ', '~~SALINITY - '
            assign norm = norm | replace: 'ACIDITY - ', '~~ACIDITY - '
            assign norm = norm | replace: 'BALANCE - ', '~~BALANCE - '
          -%}
          {%- if norm contains '~~' -%}
            {%- assign chunks = norm | split: '~~' -%}
          {%- else -%}
            {%- assign chunks = norm | split: '

' -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            step_n counts RENDERED steps, not loop iterations.

            The keyword marker is inserted before "FRUIT - ", which sits at the
            very start of the string, so split() returns an empty first element.
            It is skipped correctly by the blank test below — but forloop.index
            had already counted it, so every bottle numbered its five steps
            02–06. A counter that only advances when something is actually
            printed cannot drift out of step with what is on the page.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- assign step_n = 0 -%}
          {%- for chunk in chunks -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign clean = chunk | strip
              assign bits = clean | split: ' - '
              assign title = bits | first | strip
              assign body = clean | remove_first: title | remove_first: ' - ' | strip
            -%}
            {%- if clean != blank -%}
              {%- assign step_n = step_n | plus: 1 -%}
              {%- assign n = step_n | prepend: '0' | slice: -2, 2 -%}
              <div class="non-step">
                <div class="non-step__n">{{ n }}</div>
                <div>
                  {%- if body != blank and title.size < 40 -%}
                    <div class="non-step__t">{{ title | capitalize }}</div>
                    <p class="non-step__b">{{ body }}</p>
                  {%- else -%}
                    <p class="non-step__b">{{ clean }}</p>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Ingredients moved OUT of this column and under the gallery, in
        main-product. It is a label on a bottle, not a step in the method, and
        sitting it at the foot of the steps made the copy column taller — which
        this band pays for directly, because the film beside it is cropped to
        whatever height the copy sets. The ingredients_label setting stays here
        for now so an existing template value is not silently dropped; the
        heading itself is rendered by main-product.
      {%- endcomment -%}
    </div>

    <div class="non-process__media non-process__media--{{ media_ratio }}{% if yt_id != blank %} non-process__media--yt{% endif %}">
      {%- liquid
        assign poster = ''
        if process_image != blank
          assign poster = process_image | image_url: width: 1200
        endif
      -%}
      {%- if yt_id != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          YouTube, with the player suppressed as far as YouTube allows.

          loop=1 does nothing on its own — the API only loops a PLAYLIST, so a
          single video has to name itself as its own playlist. That is the one
          parameter everybody misses and it is why "loop" appears not to work.

          controls=0 removes the scrub bar. The title card and the share
          buttons are drawn on hover regardless of any parameter, so the iframe
          takes pointer-events: none in CSS — nothing here is clickable by
          design, it is a texture behind the process copy, and that also stops
          a stray tap sending someone to youtube.com.

          nocookie host, because this plays for every visitor without consent
          and the cookie-writing host would make it a tracking surface.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <iframe
          class="non-process__yt"
          src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/{{ yt_id }}?autoplay=1&mute=1&loop=1&playlist={{ yt_id }}&controls=0&modestbranding=1&rel=0&iv_load_policy=3&disablekb=1&fs=0&playsinline=1"
          title="{{ product.title | escape }}"
          allow="autoplay; encrypted-media"
          referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
          loading="lazy"
          tabindex="-1"
          aria-hidden="true"
          frameborder="0"></iframe>
      {%- elsif process_video_url != blank -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          A plain file URL — the Shopify Files route. Muted autoplay is the
          only kind a browser will start without a gesture, and a band behind
          copy must never grab audio. controls stay off: this is a texture,
          not a player, and there is nothing to seek.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <video
          class="non-process__img"
          autoplay
          loop
          muted
          playsinline
          preload="metadata"
          {% if poster != blank %}poster="{{ poster }}"{% endif %}
          aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }}">
          <source src="{{ process_video_url }}" type="video/mp4">
        </video>
      {%- elsif process_video.sources.size > 0 -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          A Shopify-hosted video — product media or the video picker. video_tag
          writes the whole source set, so it is preferred over hand-rolling one.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {{
          process_video
          | video_tag:
            class: 'non-process__img',
            autoplay: true,
            loop: true,
            muted: true,
            controls: false,
            image_size: '1200x'
        }}
      {%- elsif process_video.url != blank -%}
        <video
          class="non-process__img"
          autoplay
          loop
          muted
          playsinline
          preload="metadata"
          {% if poster != blank %}poster="{{ poster }}"{% endif %}
          aria-label="{{ product.title | escape }}">
          <source src="{{ process_video.url }}" type="video/mp4">
        </video>
      {%- elsif process_image != blank -%}
        {{
          process_image
          | image_url: width: 1200, format: 'webp'
          | image_tag:
            loading: 'lazy',
            widths: '600,900,1200',
            class: 'non-process__img',
            alt: product.title
        }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Loaded here rather than in theme.liquid: it has nothing to do on a page with
  no steps on it, and this is the only section that renders them.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if steps != blank or prose != blank -%}
  <script src="{{ 'steps-accordion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Process & pairings",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "steps_heading",
      "label": "Process heading",
      "default": "How it's made — not de-alcoholised"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "pairings_heading",
      "label": "Pairings heading",
      "default": "Pour it with"
    },

    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Media"
    },
    {
      "type": "video",
      "id": "video",
      "label": "Process video",
      "info": "Plays muted and looping, and replaces the image. Per-product films belong on the product's custom.process_video metafield instead — this setting applies to EVERY product, because one template renders them all."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "video_url",
      "label": "Process video file URL",
      "info": "For an .mp4 uploaded to Shopify Files: copy its URL and paste it here. Wins over every other media source. Per product, use custom.process_video_url."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Process image",
      "info": "Overrides the product's process image. Left empty, it falls back to the product's own process metafield, then its second media item, then its featured image."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "media_ratio",
      "label": "Image shape",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "square",
          "label": "Square (1:1)"
        },
        {
          "value": "tall",
          "label": "Tall (4:5)"
        },
        {
          "value": "portrait",
          "label": "Portrait (3:4)"
        },
        {
          "value": "fill",
          "label": "Fill the panel"
        }
      ],
      "default": "portrait"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "ingredients_label",
      "label": "Ingredients label",
      "default": "Ingredients"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "bg_color",
      "label": "Background"
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "text_color",
      "label": "Text colour"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "font_family",
      "label": "Font",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "",
          "label": "Theme default"
        },
        {
          "value": "sans",
          "label": "Helvetica (all text)"
        },
        {
          "value": "mono",
          "label": "JetBrains Mono (all text)"
        }
      ],
      "default": ""
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "text_scale",
      "label": "Text size",
      "min": 70,
      "max": 150,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 100,
      "info": "Scales every text size in this section together."
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "section_padding",
      "label": "Vertical padding",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 160,
      "step": 8,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0,
      "info": "0 keeps the section's own spacing."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Process & pairings"
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 30,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "step",
      "name": "Step",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Overrides the product's process_steps metafield for THIS template only. Leave the section with no Step blocks to keep using each product's own data."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "title",
          "label": "Title",
          "default": "Fruit"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "body",
          "label": "Body"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "number",
          "label": "Number",
          "info": "Optional. Auto-numbers from position when empty."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "pairing",
      "name": "Pairing card",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Overrides the product's pairings metafield for THIS template only."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "title",
          "label": "Title"
        },
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "id": "body",
          "label": "Body"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
